  <running_head>P. VOET</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>juriâ</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">qui injuriam injuriâ compen-</l>
    <l n="2">sat, semet ipsum grandi malo</l>
    <l n="3">afficit; &amp; in magnas semet in-</l>
    <l n="4">jicit calamitates. Ita enim in-</l>
    <l n="5">juriarum hinc inde non erit</l>
    <l n="6">finis; cum si semper aliquid</l>
    <l n="7">reponendum sit, semper etiam</l>
    <l n="8">supereffet ultio. Suadet hoc</l>
    <l n="9">vitæ noftræ imperfectio, in</l>
    <l n="10">quâ , cum indies peccemus</l>
    <l n="11">in proximum, adeoque alio-</l>
    <l n="12">rum opus habeamus remissio-</l>
    <l n="13">ne, æquum est, nos etiam tales</l>
    <l n="14">esse erga delinquentes, quales</l>
    <l n="15">illos erga nos peccatores ex-</l>
    <l n="16">optaremus. Suadet hoc Dei</l>
    <l n="17">facilitas erga nos in condo-</l>
    <l n="18">nandis peccatis ; qui cum sit</l>
    <l n="19">omnis expers maculæ, sæpis-</l>
    <l n="20">simeque à nobis contumeliâ</l>
    <l n="21">afficiatur, non tamen nos pro-</l>
    <l n="22">vocat, aut vindicat injurias,</l>
    <l n="23">sed ad ignoscendum se facilem</l>
    <l n="24">præbet. Cur igitur nos miseri</l>
    <l n="25">peccatores, opinione tantum</l>
    <l n="26">noftrâ, non in rei veritate in-</l>
    <l n="27">juriâ</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Catchword read as "juriâ" at the right below the last line; the hyphenated word "in-" at the line end suggests it may begin with "in". Long s rendered as plain s throughout. "quâ ," keeps the space before the comma as printed. No marginal notes or footnotes printed.</notes>
